1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. e5 Nfd7 5. f4 c5 6. dxc5 Bxc5 7. Nf3 Nc6 8. Bd3
Nb4 {? Rosselson} 9. a3 Nxd3+ 10. Qxd3 Qb6 {? wastes time - Rosselson} 11. b4
Be7 12. Be3 Qd8 13. O-O Nb6 14. Kh1 Bd7 15. b5 Rc8 16. a4 Qc7 17. Bd4 Nc4 18.
f5 Bc5 19. fxe6 Bxe6 20. Ne2 Bxd4 21. Nexd4 O-O {Looks hopeless, I suggested
Qe7 - Rosselson} 22. Ng5 g6 23. Ndxe6 fxe6 24. Qh3 (24. Rxf8+ Rxf8 25. Nxe6
Qxe5 $1 {Rosselson}) 24... Rf5 25. Nxe6 Qxe5 26. Ng5 Rc7 27. Rfe1 Ne3 {! The
only move - Rosselson} 28. Nf3 (28. Qxe3 Rf1+ $1) 28... Qf4 29. Nh4 Ng4 30. Qg3
{Forced - Rosselson} Qxg3 31. hxg3 Rh5 {? Rosselson} ({My suggestion} 31... Rf2
{leads to at least a draw - Rosselson (Stockfish 15 concurs)}) 32. Kg1 Rxc2 {
?? Rosselson} 33. Re7 Re5 34. Rxb7 g5 {?? Rosselson} (34... Ree2 {Rosselson/
Stockfish 15}) 35. Nf3 Ree2 36. Ne1 Ra2 37. Rc1 Re8 38. Rxa7 Rae2 39. Nf3 Ne3
40. b6 Rxg2+ 41. Kh1 g4 42. b7 {Source: Rosselson scoresheet. Black player DC
Martin (Ilford County Grammar School) and, in brackets, after his name, Leon
Rosselson, suggesting that the Ilford player was the principal player and
Rosselson his official/unofficial helper. Bronstein scored +18, =3, -0, while
Taimanov scored +14, =4, -3. Bronstein drew with J Penrose, PH Clarke and M
Philip Allfrey (London Boy Champion). Taimanov drew with Eileen Tranmer,
Richard H Newman, E Millis and T Sweby, and lost to L G Kennion (Essex, aged
20), B Ward (Ilford County High School) and H Alec Samuels (Cambridge
University). Played at the SCR Society, 20 Pont Street, London SW1.} 1-0

